  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n**Model tier:** low\n\n## Context\n\nModel tier rationale: One redundant mkdir and import are removed from a single test, with no runtime behavior change.\n\nHarvest issue #1099 collected the open review findings of merged pull requests. This draft covers the finding of PR #1095 at `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/tenantEntity.test.ts:64`: in `migrateAcrossThisMigration`, `await mkdir(dir, { recursive: true })` is a no-op because `mkdtemp` on line 61 already created the directory and returned its path. The `mkdir` import on line 1 is used only by that call.\n\n## Task\n\nIn `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/tenantEntity.test.ts`, delete the `await mkdir(dir, { recursive: true });` line and remove `mkdir` from the `node:fs/promises` import on line 1. Change nothing else in the file.\n\n## Touches\n- backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/tenantEntity.test.ts (the import on line 1 and the `mkdir` call at :64 only)\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n- Removing the redundant call and its now-unused import.\n\n### Out of scope\n- Any other change to `tenantEntity.test.ts` or to the migration it exercises.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `tenantEntity.test.ts` contains no `mkdir` reference.\n- `tenantEntity.test.ts` passes unchanged in behavior.\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=1095 key=0618c8c351 -->",
